        <div id="compare" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            8. Transparent Labs vs Other Isolates
          </h2>

          <p>
            Against <strong>Ascent</strong>, Transparent Labs wins on purity and loses on price. Ascent's whey is a blend of native whey isolate, regular whey isolate and some whey concentrate, at 25 g of protein per scoop, and it is Informed Sport certified. Transparent Labs is a pure isolate at 28 g. Very lactose-sensitive buyers should pick Transparent Labs. Everyone else may find Ascent's lower 4 lb price persuasive. Our <a href="/ascent-protein-powder-review/">Ascent protein review</a> goes into detail.
          </p>

          <p>
            Against <strong>Naked Nutrition</strong>, the trade is flavor and certification against simplicity. Naked's unflavored grass-fed whey isolate has only two ingredients, whey isolate and sunflower lecithin, and 30 g of protein per serving, and it now comes in a handful of flavors too. Transparent Labs offers far more flavors and Informed certification. If you mostly blend your protein, the comparison in our <a href="/naked-nutrition-protein-powder-review/">Naked Nutrition review</a> is worth a look.
          </p>

          <p>
            Against mainstream isolates like <strong>Dymatize ISO100</strong> and <strong>Isopure</strong>, Transparent Labs usually costs more. Those brands are often cheaper per gram and widely discounted, and many mainstream isolates sweeten with sucralose, so read the label on the flavor you want. If you have no objection to artificial sweeteners, they are perfectly good products and our <a href="/isopure-protein-powder-review/">Isopure review</a> explains its lineup. If you want to avoid artificial sweeteners, Transparent Labs is one of the strongest options.
          </p>

          <p>
            Against other premium certified brands like <strong>Momentous</strong> and <strong>Legion</strong>, it comes down to flavor preference and price on the day. All three sell themselves as premium, clean-label, third-party-tested brands, so compare the label and certification of the exact flavor you want. Our <a href="/momentous-protein-powder-review/">Momentous review</a> and <a href="/legion-protein-powder-review/">Legion review</a> cover those. Transparent Labs offers the widest flavor range of the three.
          </p>
